description:
Verify the transparency log's signed hourly checkpoint: the root signature against the trusted root keys, the hash chain recomputed end to end, and the checkpoint head proven to be a real entry in that chain (a checkpoint is an hourly snapshot, so its head may lag the live head — lag is consistent, a head that never existed is not). Omit checkpoint to verify the live one, or present one to check it. Authenticated callers only (rule B). Auth signature over "DAXNI-REGISTRAR-AUTH-v1
{your handle}
MCP:verify_ledger_checkpoint
/v1/checkpoint/verify
{timestamp}
aud:daxni.com" (audience-bound).
